function renderHelp(){
 const root=$('#view');root.className='doc';
 root.innerHTML=`
<h3>How budgets work</h3>
<p>Each channel gets <b>0.17 GB &times; distinct videos you watched in the last 2 weeks</b>, clamped between <code>budget_min_gb</code> and <code>budget_max_gb</code>. Hot channels rotate automatically: yosync downloads the newest uploads, then swaps out the oldest files to stay in budget.</p>
<h3>QuickFill</h3>
<p>Run <code>yosync --quickfill</code> to fill hot channels toward budget right now, using parallel workers + aria2 when present. Add <code>--logs</code> to watch it live.</p>
<h3>Watch history</h3>
<p>yosync is driven by your Google Takeout <i>watch history</i>, not subscriptions. Export it at <a href="https://takeout.google.com/settings/takeout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">takeout.google.com</a>, drop the zip into <code>.yosync/incoming/</code> (or <code>yosync --ingest &lt;zip&gt;</code>), and let it learn what you watch. Use <code>--drive</code> to pull the newest export automatically via rclone.</p>
<h3>Ad cleanup</h3>
<p>Channels you watch that turned into paid-ad slots get detected and reclaimed. You can add manual bans under Protection, and any name matching an <code>ad_keyword</code> gets purged. Channels listed in <code>exclude_channels</code> are never touched.</p>
<h3>Background sync</h3>
<p><code>yosync --daemon</code> installs a launchd agent (macOS) or a systemd user timer (Linux) that syncs daily via <code>--drive --silent</code>. Toggle with <code>--no-daemon</code>. The time is set by <code>daemon_time</code> (24-hour HH:MM) and is applied the next time you run <code>yosync --daemon</code> — changing it here does not reschedule an already-installed agent by itself. These files are set up in the raw <code>config.json</code>, but everything in this page updates them live.</p>
`;
}
function renderTrouble(){
 const root=$('#view');root.className='doc';
 root.innerHTML=`
<h3>Nothing downloads</h3>
<p>Run <code>yosync --dry-run</code> first — it prints exactly what would happen without touching your library. Check <code>logs/sync.log</code> under the library's <code>.yosync/</code> folder.</p>
<h3>Everything is stale</h3>
<p>Renew the export: download a fresh Google Takeout <i>watch history</i> zip and ingest it. Or run <code>yosync --drive</code> to pull the newest one automatically.</p>
<h3>Downloads fail</h3>
<p>YouTube rate-limits anonymous access. Add cookies (path or browser name) under QuickFill &rarr; Cookies so yt-dlp authenticates, or hand-download a video via yt-dlp to confirm the network is fine.</p>
<h3>Disk is filling up</h3>
<p>Lower <code>budget_per_video</code>, raise the pack margin, or set per-channel overrides under Budgets. Check <code>file free</code> and the Status tab.</p>
<h3>State and files disagree</h3>
<p>Run the integrity check (<code>yosync --verify</code>) — it detects missing or corrupt files and reconciles the index.</p>
<h3>youtube blocked / age-restricted</h3>
<p>Unauthenticated downloads can fail for age-restricted or region-locked videos — the cookies setting fixes most of these.</p>
<h3>Logs</h3>
<p>Every run writes <code>logs/sync.log</code>. If something breaks, read the last run there first before re-running a full sync.</p>
`;
}
